<title>USA: USDA extends GSM-102 credit to China for FY97.</title>
<headline>USDA extends GSM-102 credit to China for FY97.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department announced Monday that it has authorized $100 million in credit guarantees for sales of U.S. agricultural commodities to China under the GSM-102 program for fiscal year 1997.</p>
<p>This is the third consecutive year that USDA has authorized $100 million in credit guarantees to China. China has so far not used any of that credit.</p>
<p>The credit covers sales of animal feed products, cotton, feed grains, fish, fresh fruits, frozen or chilled meats, oilseeds, protein meals, rice, vegetable oils, wheat and wheat flour and other commodities.</p>
